  "summary": "New methods fuse predicted expression with rare-variant kernels, learn phenotype scales, ensemble PRS, and test interactions across multiple binary traits.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is genetic association and prediction that combines information sources rather than relying on marginal single-variant tests or fixed modeling choices. PrediXSKAT embeds PrediXcan-predicted expression into the SKAT kernel, jointly testing rare coding and common cis-regulatory variants to improve gene-level power. GiMat extends multivariate kernel regression to test SNP gene-gene interactions across multiple dichotomous phenotypes. SIQReg learns a phenotype scale transformation minimizing quantile heterogeneity, improving GWAS, TWAS and polygenic prediction in UK Biobank. On the prediction side, a regularized ensemble framework builds polygenic risk scores from GWAS summary statistics alone and outperforms existing PRS methods. A related preprint fine-tunes Borzoi and AlphaGenome on admixed-population genomes and RNA-seq, finding they match, rather than exceed, variant-based linear models for expression prediction, which bears on the expression-imputation step that TWAS-style approaches such as PrediXSKAT depend on. Three works are published; PrediXSKAT and the sequence-model comparison are preprints.",
